---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Plastic Circle West Africa turns discarded plastic into local jobs, everyday products and cleaner coastlines in Sierra Leone and The Gambia."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">An Ayara Foundation Switzerland programme</p>
      <h1 class="reveal">Plastic Circle West Africa</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        We turn discarded plastic into local jobs, everyday products and
        cleaner coastlines, starting in Sierra Leone and The Gambia.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta reveal">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="#platforms">See the Country Platforms</a>
        <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
      </div>

      <div class="fact-row reveal">
        <div class="fact">
          <Icon name="map" variant="inverse" />
          <div>
            <p class="fact-title">Two countries</p>
            <p class="fact-note">Sierra Leone and The Gambia</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <Icon name="gear" variant="inverse" />
          <div>
            <p class="fact-title">One shared model</p>
            <p class="fact-note">From collection to local manufacturing</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <Icon name="users" variant="inverse" />
          <div>
            <p class="fact-title">Local teams</p>
            <p class="fact-note">Run day to day by local implementation partners</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card-head reveal">
        <Icon name="wave" />
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:0.2em;">The challenge</p>
          <h2 style="margin:0;">Plastic is piling up across West Africa's coasts and cities</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="max-width: 760px;">
        Plastic waste collects faster than fast-growing coastal cities in
        West Africa can manage it. Much of it never reaches a bin or a
        recycling facility. It ends up in drains, rivers, mangroves and the
        ocean, where it harms wildlife, blocks drainage and raises public
        health risks in crowded neighbourhoods.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal" style="max-width: 760px;">
        Worldwide, people produce more than 400 million tonnes of plastic
        every year, and a large share of it becomes waste (UNEP, 2024). In
        West Africa, limited collection systems and small-scale recycling
        turn that waste into a daily, visible problem on streets and
        beaches.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal" style="max-width: 760px;">
        Plastic Circle West Africa treats that same plastic as a local
        resource. Collected, sorted and processed close to where it is
        generated, it becomes furniture, household goods and income for the
        people who collect and make it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The model</p>
        <h2>From waste leakage to local value creation</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="truck" />
            <h3>Recover</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Neighbourhood and institutional collection, local collectors,
            labelled drop-off points and public campaigns create a reliable
            plastic feedstock.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="filter" />
            <h3>Prepare</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Plastic is sorted by type, colour and quality, then cleaned and
            prepared for production under clear quality and safety
            procedures.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="gear" />
            <h3>Make</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Locally operated machinery shreds, presses and forms recovered
            plastic into furniture, outdoor products, interior elements,
            surfaces, household goods and customised products.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="bag" />
            <h3>Sell &amp; Reinvest</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Product sales and services create local revenue, with surpluses
            reinvested into operations, jobs, maintenance and gradual
            expansion.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" id="platforms" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--blush);">Country platforms</p>
      <h2>Two local platforms, one shared approach</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Plastic Loop</strong> in The Gambia and <strong>DecoPlastic</strong>
        in Sierra Leone apply the same model on the ground, each shaped by
        its own local partner, waste streams and markets.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid cols-2 reveal">
      <a class="platform-card" href={`${base}sierra-leone`} style="color:inherit;">
        <div class="platform-head">
          <span class="country">Sierra Leone</span>
          <h3 style="margin:0;">DecoPlastic</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-body">
          <p>
            Led by Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions, working across
            Freetown and the wider country.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">See local data and the team &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="platform-card" href={`${base}gambia`} style="color:inherit;">
        <div class="platform-head">
          <span class="country">The Gambia</span>
          <h3 style="margin:0;">Plastic Loop</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-body">
          <p>
            Led by Hustle for Humanity Gambia, working across the Greater
            Banjul Area.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">See local data and the team &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Impact at a glance</p>
        <h2>Six ways this programme creates value</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="droplet" />
            <h3>Cleaner waters &amp; biodiversity</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Plastic kept out of rivers, mangroves and coastal waters, protecting aquatic and marine life.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="recycle" />
            <h3>Circular economy, less waste</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Plastic recovered, reused and made into products, cutting demand for virgin material.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="briefcase" />
            <h3>Decent work &amp; local value</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Local green jobs and income, with collectors fairly integrated and better earnings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="users" />
            <h3>Women &amp; youth included</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Clear targets for women's participation and a strong focus on young people.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="home" />
            <h3>Healthier communities</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Cleaner neighbourhoods, better waste management and lower public health risks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="leaf" />
            <h3>Climate action</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Less open burning of plastic and protection of carbon-storing mangroves.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="message" />
            <h3>Awareness &amp; dialogue</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Public campaigns and community engagement build lasting awareness of plastic pollution and why recycling matters.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Focus</p>
        <h2>Four dimensions of impact</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid cols-2 reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="droplet" />
            <h3>Environmental</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Plastic diverted from drains, rivers, mangroves and coasts and
            converted into productive use, with less open burning along the
            way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="users" />
            <h3>Social</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Inclusive jobs, training and safer, more structured
            participation for collectors, with deliberate targets for women
            and young people, alongside public campaigns that build
            community awareness of plastic pollution and recycling.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="chart" />
            <h3>Economic</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            A local value chain from waste to product, growing revenue,
            buyers and services over time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="bolt" />
            <h3>Operational</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Resilient production through hybrid energy, quality control and
            durable local partnerships and sourcing agreements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our partners</p>
        <h2>Who delivers the programme</h2>
        <p>
          Plastic Circle West Africa is delivered through a Swiss-led
          partnership with a shared technology partner, backed by local
          implementation organisations on the ground in each country.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="building" />
            <h3>Ayara Foundation Switzerland</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Programme lead: strategy, technical direction, governance and
            international partnerships, in close collaboration with the
            local lead partners.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="gear" />
            <h3>ECOLLABO8</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Technology partner: recycling machinery, technical onboarding,
            production know-how and training for local teams.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="bolt" />
            <h3>ETH Zurich</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Recycling and production quality support, process design and
            applied know-how from an academic angle, complementing
            ECOLLABO8's machinery and training.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
        Each country platform also has its own local implementation partner
        on the ground. See the <a class="text-link" href={`${base}sierra-leone`}>Sierra Leone</a>
        and <a class="text-link" href={`${base}gambia`}>Gambia</a> pages for details.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="positions" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card-head reveal">
        <Icon name="briefcase" />
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:0.2em;">Open positions</p>
          <h2 style="margin:0;">Join a local team</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="max-width: 760px;">
        As each country platform moves from setup into operations, our
        local implementation partners are building local teams in
        collection, production, design, finance and community engagement.
        Roles below are recruited in anticipation of donor approval. More
        positions will be added as Sierra Leone and The Gambia scale up.
      </p>

      <div class="job-list reveal">
        <div class="job-item">
          <div class="job-main">
            <h3>Senior Finance and Administrative Officer</h3>
            <p>
              Greater Banjul Area &middot; full-time, 12-month contract,
              renewable
            </p>
            <p>
              Oversees financial management and administrative operations
              for the project: budgeting, financial reporting, donor
              compliance, procurement and general office administration.
            </p>
            <div class="job-tags">
              <span class="tag">The Gambia</span>
              <span class="tag">Finance &amp; Admin</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="job-apply">
            <a class="text-link" href="mailto:plasticloopgambia@gmail.com?subject=Senior%20Finance%20and%20Administrative%20Officer">Apply by email &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="job-item">
          <div class="job-main">
            <h3>Workshop Fabrication Lead</h3>
            <p>
              Greater Banjul Area &middot; full-time, 12-month contract,
              renewable
            </p>
            <p>
              Coordinates and supervises workshop fabrication activities,
              keeping production safe, efficient and in line with approved
              drawings, specifications and quality standards.
            </p>
            <div class="job-tags">
              <span class="tag">The Gambia</span>
              <span class="tag">Production</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="job-apply">
            <a class="pill-btn outline" href={`${base}documents/workshop-fabrication-lead-gambia.docx`}>Download Job Description</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="more-note reveal">More roles will be posted here as recruitment opens for DecoPlastic in Sierra Leone and as Plastic Loop Gambia scales up.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); text-align:center;">
    <h2>Want to learn more or get involved</h2>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin: 0 auto 1.5em;">
      Get in touch to learn more about Plastic Circle West Africa, our
      local partners, or how to support the work in Sierra Leone and The
      Gambia.
    </p>
    <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark {
    border-color: var(--blush);
    color: var(--blush-pale);
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark:hover {
    background: var(--blush-pale);
    color: var(--wine-dark);
  }

  .job-list {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .job-apply {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .more-note {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
